This software program—known as **BridgeCraft** (formerly titled *"The Behavioral Profiler"*), including its source code, architecture, user interface design, scoring algorithms, and accompanying documentation (collectively, the **"Software"**), is the sole, original, and exclusive intellectual property of **Jack Likert** (the **"Author"**).

1. **Independent Creation:** The Software was conceived, designed, developed, and reduced to practice entirely on the Author's personal, non-work time, utilizing exclusively personal equipment, personal software licenses, and personal resources, without the use of any employer, client, or third-party facilities, equipment, supplies, confidential information, trade secrets, or funding.
2. **Not a Work Made for Hire:** Under no circumstances shall the Software, or any portion thereof, be construed or deemed a "work made for hire" under the United States Copyright Act (17 U.S.C. § 101) or any international equivalent.
3. **Pre-Existing & Excluded Intellectual Property:** This Software constitutes a pre-existing, excluded personal invention under any Proprietary Information and Inventions Agreement (PIIA), non-compete, or employment agreement to which the Author may be or become a party.

